\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec4 Overall your data and methods look good, a few comments:\
1) Just to be clear, your output variable is a binary value for each pixel (yes there was fire or no there is no fire), correct? So you will be doing random forest classification?\
2) Since your output is a binary class, you might want to consider also running logistic regression, as a comparison to random forest classification:\
https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression.html\
3) I don't see any mention of tuning the hyperparameters of your random forest model. Make sure you do include this. Machine learning models like random forest can easily get over-fit if you don't properly tune the model with something like Grid Search CV.\
4) I like your sensitivity discussion, it would be good to include this in your final project.\cell 
